		<profileDesc>
			<abstract>
				<p>In this work, we propose DOUBLEDIPPER, a novel In-Context-Learning method that automatically generates few-shot examples for several QA tasks by recycling contexts. Specifically, given an input context (1-3k tokens) and a query, we generate additional query-output pairs from the given context as few-shot examples, while introducing the context only once. This ensures that the demonstrations are leveraging the same context as the target query while only adding a small number of tokens to the prompt. We further enhance each demonstration by instructing the model to explicitly identify the relevant paragraphs before the answer, which improves performance while providing fine-grained attribution to the answer source. We apply our method on multiple LLMs and obtain substantial improvements (+16 absolute points on average across models) on various QA datasets. Surprisingly, despite introducing only single-hop ICL examples, LLMs successfully generalize to multi-hop QA using our approach.</p>
			</abstract>
		</profileDesc>
